<http://data.silknow.org/object/f5eac3f9-343f-3688-a76c-098eec4330a0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Loom-width of brocaded silk with floral meanders. The main pattern of semi-naturalistic flowers, arranged in symmetrical floral meanders, is brocaded in silks ranging in colour from peach through tan to dark red, white and bright green, and in silver thread filé and frisé. The ground is of blue ribbed silk with a portion of the weft used to form ground patterns of diaper and striped fillings, flowers and leaves which follow the lines of the main brocaded pattern. Six white silk cords form the selvedge."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f5eac3f9-343f-3688-a76c-098eec4330a0> .

